    "explanation": "Trip TRP-00109 (Clementi MRT to Bukit Batok MRT). Disputed amount SGD 12.00. The rider's fare stands and the driver is paid SGD 3.15.\n\n1. THE RAW DEVIATION IS REAL BUT IT IS THE DETOUR THE RIDER ASKED FOR. The platform optimal was 6.40 km / 14.0 min (EV-TRIP-00109); the GPS trace measured 13.76 km (EV-GPS-00109), so the raw excess is 7.36 km, 115% of optimal — above both POL-RD-01 gates and material. POL-RD-01, however, assesses materiality on the excess REMAINING after a POL-RD-04 adjustment. At 18:22:06, about a minute after the meter started at 18:21:10, the chat log records the rider's own message 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min' (EV-CHAT-00109, MSG-00109-001), from the rider account, with a resolved waypoint_hint for Jurong Point (VEN-JURONG-POINT). That satisfies POL-RD-04(a), (b) and (c) without any geocoding. The trace corroborates it: the nearest fix to that waypoint is 37.94 m away, inside the 200 m threshold, and the vehicle was stationary there for 366 s (EV-GPS-00109), matching the rider's '5 min' and her 'coming down now' at 18:35:40. Nothing on the trace shows any departure from the optimal corridor other than that requested stop, so the whole 7.36 km excess is excluded and no deviation is established. POL-RD-02 therefore does not run and no distance-or-time refund is due: the arithmetic the rider's advocate offered — charged_total 21.32 less recomputed_fare 13.32 = 8.00 — is correct as arithmetic but is not payable, because the deviation that would trigger it is exonerated. The rider's argument that the exonerated portion is unmeasurable is rejected: the record identifies one departure and one cause, so the off-corridor excess is the measured excess, and the rider's fallback request to escalate under POL-RD-10 is refused for the same reason, no POL-RD-10 limb having fired.\n\n2. THE DRIVER WAS UNDER-BILLED AND IS COMPENSATED. The fare breakdown charges for 9.60 km (EV-FARE-00109) while the trace records 13.76 km — a shortfall of 4.16 km, above the 1.0 km trigger in POL-RD-04. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is SGD 3.12, rounded UP to SGD 3.15, within the SGD 15.00 cap. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries that same SGD 3.15; the rider's contested charge stands.\n\n3. POINTS ANSWERED TOGETHER. Trace integrity: both sides agree and the record confirms the trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 (207 fixes, 10 s interval, no gaps, maximum gap 0 s), so no POL-RD-07(ii) corroboration and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arise, and POL-RD-14 is not engaged because the trace did corroborate the instruction. Traffic: no traffic cause was asserted by either party, so POL-RD-03 is not invoked; the missing advisory EV-ADVIS-00109-01 (MISSING, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, weight 0.0) is disclosed and decides nothing, and POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-10(5) do not fire. Driver profile: POL-RD-06 was consulted and no pattern is established — deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 511 completed trips in 90 days — so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. Burden: the rider did discharge the POL-RD-08 initial burden from an unimpaired trace, shifting it to the driver, who discharged it with a specific artifact and clause (EV-CHAT-00109 with POL-RD-04); the rider's own profile (deviation_claims_60d = 1) does not engage the heightened corroboration test, so her claim was not denied on that basis. Pass-throughs: the fare carries no ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to refund and produces no referral. Confidence: every artifact carrying a deciding fact — the chat log, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown — is at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and no POL-GEN-02(3) naming is required. Execution: the monetary effect (SGD 3.15) is below the POL-GEN-05 threshold of SGD 8.00, so it executes automatically. Precedents P-0001 and P-0002 are PARTIAL_REFUND under POL-RD-01/02/08; this case differs because the chat log's resolved waypoint_hint, corroborated on the driving trace to within 37.94 m, exonerates the detour under POL-RD-04 before POL-RD-02 is reached."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{"ruling":{"ruling":"DRIVER_COMPENSATION","amount_sgd":3.15,"driver_compensation_sgd":3.15,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.9,"explanation":"To the rider: your trip ran Clementi to Bukit Batok and you say 13.8 km and $21.32 are not reasonable for a 6 km trip. The record shows you asked for the detour. Chat message MSG-00109-001 on EV-CHAT-00109, sent by you at 18:22:06, one minute after the meter started at 18:21:10, reads 'hi can stop at jurong point first? need to grab something 5 min', and the platform resolved it to the Jurong Point PHV pickup point (waypoint_hint). Your driver agreed. EV-GPS-00109 shows the vehicle passing within 38 m of that waypoint (POL-RD-04's threshold is 200 m) and standing there about six minutes, matching your own '5 min' and your 'coming down now' at 18:35:40. Under POL-RD-04 the detour you requested is excluded from the deviation measure. Once excluded, nothing qualifying remains: the trace's 13.76 km against the booked optimal of 6.40 km (excess 7.36 km) is the out-and-back to the stop you asked for, and the record identifies no other departure from the corridor. No deviation is established under POL-RD-01, POL-RD-02 does not run, and the charge stands. The $8.00 refund figure you advanced (charged_total 21.32 less recomputed_fare 13.32) is rejected because POL-RD-02 only runs on an established, unexcused deviation, and your argument that the exonerated distance cannot be quantified so the case must escalate is rejected too: POL-RD-04 requires trace corroboration, which exists to within 38 m, and POL-RD-14 confirms this is not the POL-RD-10(7) contradiction, because a request that was made and a route that followed it are consistent with each other.

To the driver: your POL-RD-04 exoneration is accepted, and the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07 (207 fixes, 10 s interval, zero gaps). You are also right that the platform under-billed. EV-FARE-00109 charged 9.60 km while EV-GPS-00109 recorded 13.76 km, a shortfall of 4.16 km, above the 1.0 km trigger. At SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre that is SGD 3.12, rounded UP to SGD 3.15, inside the SGD 15.00 cap. You are granted DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.15; the rider's fare is not disturbed, and on a DRIVER_COMPENSATION ruling amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.15 (POL-GEN-03).

Points answered together: the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check returns no pattern (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0, so neither the 3-flag limb nor the 0.05 ratio over 511 completed trips is met), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral; no adverse finding rests on any context-only profile field. The absent traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00109-01 (MISSING, weight 0.0, MISSING_ARTIFACT) carries nothing here, because neither side relies on a traffic cause, so POL-RD-13 applies and no POL-RD-10(5) trigger fires. No ERP, toll or airport-surcharge lines exist, so POL-RD-09 refunds nothing. No escalation trigger in POL-RD-10 is met. Confidence 0.90: the deciding facts (your chat instruction, the trace, the fare ledger) all sit on full-weight artifacts EV-CHAT-00109, EV-GPS-00109 and EV-FARE-00109 at 1.0. The SGD 3.15 effect is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold (POL-GEN-05) and executes on issue. This differs from precedents P-0001 and P-0002, which ruled PARTIAL_REFUND, because there no rider-requested, trace-corroborated detour brought POL-RD-04 into play."},"discarded_claims":[]}

